                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Romance with Chocolate is the second game from Russian developer, Crisp App Studio, and follows in the steps of their previous Steam release with another \"adventureless\" hidden object title for those who prefer a little less point 'n' click in their HOGs.  While I'm not quite as taken with this game as compared to Time Trap, it still has a certain amount of charm despite an unpolished translation...and the soundtrack is lovely.\n\nGameplay is simply picking out items from a list of words or silhouttes.  If you're looking to 100% achievements, you'll need to play each level over and over again to decrease the time it takes to finish them and earn 3 stars, but I found this to be enjoyable enough.  Leaderboards are also available for those who like to challenge themselves competitively, which is something not often done in the genre.  \n\nMy biggest gripe is with the lack of graphical fidelity.  It is clear that the images were upscaled from a lower resolution, and thus many items are blurry and hard to distinguish.  The ability to play in windowed mode would have helped with this issue some, but sadly it's not an option.\n\nThat said, the enjoyment I received from this little title outweighed the issues I had with it's presentation, and it's a fairly easy 100% to boot.  Your mileage may vary, but it's worth checking out if you enjoyed Time Trap or are looking for more straight HOGs here on Steam.\n\n[code][h1]Curated by: [url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/33004802-Chudah%27s-Corner/]Chudah's Corner[/url][/h1][/code]",
